  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_d0d112a609a14042b5b44aebf67bdf2f",
      "statement": "The object store must provide a conditional create, a conditional overwrite, and read-after-write consistency for both promises to hold; qualified stores are Amazon S3, Cloudflare R2, Tigris, Google Cloud Storage, and Azure Blob Storage.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L16-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:63b9f9cfab832c55c5983ed79994404f5dc5d0db229214de3f829128d46e7ceb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6ab287bc598c44929300a631471cbda6",
      "statement": "A startup storage probe sends four conditional writes to the bucket and requires two of them to fail; each node repeats the test once at startup and stops on a broken store.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L60-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:34430d1673d62a38bf7f5837768ec254ebd5529438e33807e8934224aab4080e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1afa0b547f1c4140932cc0455625c7e7",
      "statement": "Conditional-write dialect is provider-specific: S3-compatible buckets use If-None-Match/If-Match etag headers, gs:// uses the Cloud Storage XML API generation precondition with OAuth, and az:// uses the same If- headers on Put Blob; only AlreadyExists and Precondition are clean rejections, every other error is ambiguous.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L43-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:887630c27d0a39fe2d638e575fa421d7f9e3aebb600c74d0e56bc794759b2eb6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9db91484062e41b08ea6f11f09e16721",
      "statement": "Each cell has one ownership record in the bucket naming the owner node session and a fencing epoch; a node acquires it with a conditional write, and every activation advances the epoch so an epoch never has two writers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L108-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:867aa55245397481450b264390ce610cbe84b9e7919c828124b722c7f1c2df98:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8e318615ab1840ce8e58f411f3cb8bc5",
      "statement": "The replicator writes each cell's SQLite data under cells/<cell>/ltx/e<epoch>/ with unconditional PUTs; the epoch in the key is the fence that keeps a stale owner's writes in a superseded prefix.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ltx_repl.rs#L9-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e5fd77dfd54d80c86345889b819dd76655ac1c4ccc646c442c33fe38595381cc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L122-L124",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:754921579ce9a34b910c32591e86b6878a4828deb203a96ff2c700f8ddbdf123:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7dd348b9218441a1bfff6f211e8853d7",
      "statement": "The acknowledgement rule holds each write response until a durability proof covers it: after a bucket proof the ownership record is read and the write is acknowledged only if it still names this node at this epoch; a fleet proof instead requires every follower to fsync and a takeover to seal the prior node-log session.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L132-L148",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e99f2d15ef8389ab0fc1d158e4585e42010257d196d763cbd96e3ad69746660d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_977773b959fe4a8997d7f27eaae993a0",
      "statement": "The output gate is one choke point every egress passes through and withholds a response until every write it can reveal is proven durable; CELLD_OUTPUT_GATE=0 removes the replication wait and accepts possible loss of an acknowledged write.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L3-L4",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b003cea6544c382eea6b71885ad1205ad303136d28d12f5ef8e9943ce7ac41f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L690-L690",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:38e60f2dd8c177a0b42aeb4041f61ba83141baae9b89a328040046fe57d96b95:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3c8878482e1c4070bbd0b5363b7ae716",
      "statement": "The default durability posture is fleet: a node needs two running nodes before any write can complete a fleet proof, recruits up to two followers, and without an ensemble acknowledges on a bucket proof instead.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L151-L167",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eb245ff4ad1ea390df353aa38d2ebb6a52afc2733b5578dff742499c2e66d139:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0c48a63399af4c0a839c958f168c3009",
      "statement": "Under fleet durability, each node streams per-cell L0 LTX segments to a follower ensemble and a write acknowledges when every member holds it or when the bucket upload proves it first; log/<node>.json is the CAS-guarded root of truth and is created before the first fleet-durable ack and never deleted.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/node_log.rs#L3-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:51e90bdc048f8cdba4cbdb2a7ebb4fa1e9b7b3b416dcba2c0ff410cb0e5bba47:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_acac5766c6484770a6ecf3222c83629f",
      "statement": "A cold activation checks the prior owner's log records before reading the bucket: an absent record proves the bucket is complete, a sealed record proves recovery completed, and an open or recovering record requires recovery (fencing, sealing followers, uploading retained segments) before the cell may restore.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L171-L183",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:434e5d50bfec9462760f50b3cba859fe88436a4de686dcc2dbaa0ad5e5ede338:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3ee223629f184baba48ac58c255aab3b",
      "statement": "A restore selects the newest epoch prefix containing LTX data and reads the full contiguous chain from transaction zero, because a later node-log recovery or bundle drain can add an acknowledged tail after an earlier restore.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L186-L198",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a0c262477b00278f6d24471b232558f653fae532889d8b123b2ba96c6edcba90:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c9585dc2a39c42019b3617ea3166d1f1",
      "statement": "A node that cannot renew its lease fences itself when its published expiry passes: it stops active cells, fails incomplete requests, writes nothing to the bucket, and exits with code 3 under a SELF-FENCE: log line; a node whose lease record was replaced fences at once.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L200-L224",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ceecdff1e02f2c68eec0e7cd0636ebf9b65f8c267c20a6cfbe950ec62f758f3f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7da79681c714489c9352a8639e6dc898",
      "statement": "celld-ltx provides embeddable streaming replication for SQLite (WAL capture as LTX segments, replica storage, restore, compaction, bundles) and is a Rust reimplementation of Litestream v0.5.11 behavior with the LTX v0.5.2 block format, vendored and owned by celld.",
